"""
hero_parser.py - Zero-Config Dynamic Hero Discovery & Real-Time Roster Sync.

Reverse-engineered from live wire captures (session 6b4f8031, Sep 19, 2026):
- Opcode 1201 (S->C, dispatched right after the 14 -> 15 login handshake):
  Full unlocked commander catalogue (~21KB). Each entry carries
  hero_id, level, star, skills (repeated), awakened flag.
- Opcode 1157 (S->C): supplemental roster confirmation list; entries shaped
  {1: hero_id, 4: level} (385 items observed on live login of NUCROSHOP).
- Opcode 1002 (S->C): city state packet.
  * Tags 9 / 12 (and submessage-form Tag 15) contain commander containers;
    hero entries found there are heroes currently ASSIGNED to a duty
    (Wall / City Garrison) -> tagging them is_wall_garrison prevents Error 135.
  * Tag 15 as a plain varint = highest unlocked (defeated) barbarian level
    (ground truth: Tag 15 = 6 on Level 17 farm accounts; attacking above it
    returns Error 1021).

This module is PURE (no network, no DB at import time) so it is unit-testable.
DB persistence is exposed via persist_roster_to_db() with lazy imports.
"""

import os
import sys
import json
import time
import logging
from typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Set

